<BaseLayout title="Zero-downtime API deployments — Amit P Madakatti" description="A serverless release pattern using Lambda versions, API Gateway traffic shifting, CloudWatch alarms and SNS notifications.">
<main class="case-page"><a class="back-link" href="/work/">← ALL WORK</a><span class="eyebrow">CASE 04 / RELEASE ENGINEERING / 2026</span><h1>Zero-downtime<br/><em>API deployments.</em></h1><p class="case-lead">Progressive Lambda releases with health monitoring and automated operational alerts.</p><div class="case-cover cover-pink"><div class="release-steps"><span>v1 / 100%</span><span>v2 / 10%</span><span>v2 / 50%</span><span>v2 / 100%</span></div></div><div class="case-meta"><div><span>ROLE</span><b>Cloud & Release Engineering</b></div><div><span>STACK</span><b>AWS Lambda · API Gateway · CloudWatch · SNS</b></div><div><span>YEAR</span><b>2026</b></div></div><div class="case-content"><section><span class="eyebrow">01 / THE BRIEF</span><h2>Change production<br/><em>with control.</em></h2><p>Move API versions through staged traffic shifts while watching operational signals.</p></section><section><span class="eyebrow">02 / THE BUILD</span><h2>Progressive traffic.<br/>Fast signals.</h2><p>Configured Lambda/API Gateway blue-green and canary release patterns in 10% steps. CloudWatch monitors 4xx/5xx spikes and SNS delivers alerts.</p></section><section><span class="eyebrow">03 / THE OUTCOME</span><h2>Visibility before<br/><em>blast radius.</em></h2><p>The design aims to detect abnormal API behaviour quickly and notify operators so they can halt or reverse a release.</p><p>CloudWatch alarms provide the health signal, while SNS provides the notification path. The release decision remains tied to observed error behaviour rather than relying only on a deployment command completing successfully.</p></section><section><span class="eyebrow">04 / RELEASE SAFETY</span><h2>Promote in stages.<br/><em>Keep a rollback path.</em></h2><p>The intended progression moves a small share of traffic to the new Lambda version, checks the monitored signals, and increases exposure only when the release remains healthy. A failed health check should stop promotion and return traffic to the known-good version.</p><p>This page documents the release approach and its intended operational controls. It does not claim a measured production incident rate, an uptime guarantee or a deployed production service.</p></section></div><a class="case-repo" href="https://github.com/amit-cloudops-ai/https-github.com-Amitpm8-aws-zero-downtime-deployment" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">VIEW SOURCE REPOSITORY ↗</a></main>
</BaseLayout>
